# Data-first extensibility

KDEM / DEMO ONE / ILS 27 are the **shipped fixture**, not the type system. A second STAR, SID, approach, or airport of an **existing schema shape** must work from JSON without a new `if`.

## Data, not a branch in FMS

| Add | Touch |
| --- | --- |
| STAR/SID/approach/fix/navaid on an existing facility | `src/scenario/data/<icao>/` (and video-maps / scenario spawn JSON if you want it on the scope) |
| New playable airport | same catalog + scenario + MAPS + MVA folders; **do not** add `loadKdem3()` — register by id / glob like `loadCatalog` |
| New **behavior** (hold, RNAV fly-by, SID runway transition, non-VECTORS termination) | schema field + generic walker; still no facility id switch |

Runtime walks `catalog.stars` / `sids` / `approaches` / `fixes` **by id**. Parser tokens (`DCT`, `VIA`, `APP`) stay generic. DCT-join, VIA, loc/GS, spawn-on-STAR already do this.

```ts
// BAD — second STAR or airport needs a code edit
if (starId === "DEM1") return ["NEMAX", "NELBO", "NJOIN", "MERGE"];

// GOOD — any catalog row
starRouteFixIds(catalog, starId, transitionId);
procedureRouteContainingFix(catalog, fixId, preferStarId);
```

## Allowed KDEM in tests and copy

Tests, F1 examples, and comments may say KDEM. **Do not** put `"KDEM"`, `"DEM1"`, `"ILS27"`, or `DEMO_ONE_NORTH_FIX_IDS` on a live path except as a documented last-resort default when the loaded catalog omits a field (SSA altimeter stub, MSAW RW27 fallback). A second facility must read the scenario/catalog instead of inheriting those stubs.

Ambiguous fixes (same id on two STARs): prefer current `PROCEDURE` / `VIA`, else first catalog hit. Do not special-case DEM1.
